WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.450
A cold, dark morning.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.230
The headlights are on,
and you turn the key.

3
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.810
As the starter motor
turns the engine over,

4
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.100
the headlights visibly dim.

5
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.620
The motor and the headlights
both run from the same battery.

6
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.940
So why should the headlights dim
the moment the motor starts to turn?

7
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.540
In this mission, you'll pin down
what a battery's emf really means:

8
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.570
the energy it gives
each coulomb of charge.

9
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:31.000
Then you'll work out the current that a
1.5 volt cell drives through a 2.5 ohm

10
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.080
resistor.

11
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:36.830
Your mission: explain why the headlights
dim as the starter motor turns.
